speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, under the provisions of Standing Order 43, and as a Canadian M.P., member of the parliamentary group Canada-Senegal Friendship, I ask the unanimous consent of the House to move an important motion.
In view of the visit today in Ottawa of His Excellency Leopold Sedar Senghor, President of the Republic of Senegal, who is in Canada as the honorary president of the World Federation of Twinned Cities, an international non governmental organization endeavouring to draw together the various nations of the world; since tomorrow, at the official opening of the Olympic village in Montreal, His Excellency, who is a keen champion and promoter of a universal brotherly civilization, will proceed with the symbolic twinning of the Olympic village with the cities of the world, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Beauce (Mr. Caron);
That the House convey to His Excellency Leopold Sedar Senghor the pleasure caused by his visit and say to him that Canadian government members join with him in his intense desire to see real bonds of friendship and cooperation develop between the peoples of the world and finally, on the occasion of the symbolic twinning of the Olympic village with the cities of the world, that the House earnestly press His Excellency to transmit to all nations the message of friendship of Canada, which really demonstrated in the past a sincere desire to establish friendly international cooperation and which endorses the various positive ways of bringing people together, including the creation of bonds between municipalities.

The article went on to say;
(It's said by some of the MPs in attendance that the comments were too close to the bone-Joe was not amused.)
Apparently I got to Joe's bone again tonight.
